Today is {{environment_date}}. {{name}} writes to you:

> Do my {{tax_year}} taxes.

Everything you can see of {{name}}'s life is in this environment: the email inbox, the websites {{name}} has accounts with (the `Portals` folder shows what each site displays, including tax forms posted there), documents, the calendar and text messages.

## How to work

Use only the `tab` command:

    tab ls [PATH]            list a folder
    tab tree                 list every file
    tab read PATH [--page N] read a file (PDFs come back as text)
    tab search PATTERN       search all files, PDFs included
    tab inbox                list the emails
    tab open URL             open a link
    tab ask "QUESTION"       ask {{name}} something
    tab write PATH < FILE    save a file (only under {{writable_folder}}/)
    tab submit PATH          submit your return (a JSON file you saved with tab write)
    tab status               show the environment status
    tab wait --days N        let time pass (mail dated by then arrives)
    tab request-approval "SUMMARY"   show {{name}} your submitted return and ask to file and pay
    tab efile                e-file the return you submitted (after {{name}} approves it)
    tab pay --to PAYEE --amount N --from ACCOUNT   pay from one of {{name}}'s bank accounts

Work only from what you find here and from {{name}}'s answers. Don't invent facts. Act as a careful tax preparer would.

## Filing and paying

`tab request-approval` shows {{name}} your latest submission and asks for the OK. `tab efile` files the latest submission, and only if {{name}} has approved it. `tab pay` pays from one of {{name}}'s bank accounts (give its account number).

## What to submit

Save a JSON file under `{{writable_folder}}/` and submit it with `tab submit`. You can resubmit; only the last submission counts.

    {
      "persona_id": "{{id}}",
      "tax_year": {{tax_year}},
      "forms": {
        "f1040": { "1a": 12345, "...": 0 },
        "...": {}
